After nine years of active nethacking I thought that I'd seen almost
every way to die. Yesterday proved me wrong. I know that I was
tempting the fate when I started a healer after my record streak of
four consequtive ascensions (monk, 2 wizards, and valkyrie). But the
precise way of dying still surprised me.

I advanced a little too quick and carelessly, and found myself in
Sokoban battling against giant ants without having weapon and armor
good enough. There was only one ant left and it had cornered me in a
place where I couldn't escape, I quaffed the last one of the extra
healing potions from the starting equipment:

 "As you open the bottle, an enormous ghost emerges" -more-
 "You are frightened to death, and unable to move."

Goodbye TSS, killed by a hill-orc while helpless. 

I was surprised that it wasn't the ant who nailed me, that orc stepped
beside the ant while I was paralyzed.

